# The Linux packaging revision: "<app version> <revision>".
#
# Bump the revision when the .deb, the tarball or the APT repository has to be rebuilt while the
# app itself is unchanged (a dependency, an installed file, the metainfo, the systemd unit), so the
# new package has a version of its own and never replaces the published files of the same name. It
# applies only while the app version matches: once tauri.conf.json moves to a new version, packages
# are that version again with no suffix, whatever this file says. tools/linux/package-version.sh
# reads it, and build-deb.sh re-stamps the .deb's control Version with the result.
#
# Nothing is active yet. The first entry would look like:
#
#   1.0.0 2
